4. One issue I noticed in your current code

You currently have:

disabled: !entity.active,

This applies to Customer, Billing Group AND Location.

So if your requirement is still what you mentioned earlier — inactive locations should be disabled, but Customers and Billing Groups should not be affected — then you should change this too.

Use:

disabled:
  type === AddPanelType.Location
    ? entity.active === false
    : false,

So the complete method becomes:

private generateDropdownOptions(
  entities: ContextEntity[],
  type: AddPanelType
) {
  return entities.map((entity: any) => ({
    value: entity,

    viewValue:
      type === AddPanelType.BillingGroup
        ? `${entity.name} (${(entity as BillingGroup).billingGroupId})`
        : entity.name,

    // Disable inactive options only for Location
    disabled:
      type === AddPanelType.Location
        ? entity.active === false
        : false,

    // Tooltip only for Location
    tooltip:
      type === AddPanelType.Location
        ? entity.facilityId
        : undefined,
  }));
}

This gives you exactly:

Dropdown	Inactive	Disabled	Tooltip

Customer	Yes	❌ No	❌ No
Customer	No	❌ No	❌ No
Billing Group	Yes	❌ No	❌ No
Billing Group	No	❌ No	❌ No
Location	Yes	✅ Yes	✅ ID
Location	No	❌ No	✅ ID


So you don't need to touch updateDropdown() either. It already calls generateDropdownOptions(), meaning newly added Locations will automatically receive the tooltip and disabled state.